// W7-04 U1b/t, S-811: the candidate of `sample_rate!()`, the name of a flow that is called without `~` (§11.4), removes the `!` (§11.2), and the
// file has no error after it (`clean`; `sample_tick()` is the E0200 of a later stage in this version, so only `sample_rate` is here).



pub flow call(x: F32 at sample) -> F32 at sample {
  sample_rate!() * x                                //~ E0806
}
